    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "display": "$\\dfrac{15}{17}$",
      "correct": false,
      "note": "$\\sin A$, the given ratio",
      "why": "$\\frac{15}{17}$ is opposite ÷ hypotenuse for angle $A$, which is $\\sin A$ (the given ratio); $\\tan B$ needs opposite ÷ adjacent, $\\frac{8}{15}$.",
      "rationale": "Repeats the given sin A instead of finding tan B."
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "display": "$\\dfrac{15}{8}$",
      "correct": false,
      "note": "$\\tan A$: sides seen from angle $A$",
      "why": "$\\frac{15}{8}$ uses the opposite and adjacent sides relative to angle $A$, not angle $B$, so it is $\\tan A$; $\\tan B$ is $\\frac{8}{15}$.",
      "rationale": "Computes tan A: opposite and adjacent taken from the wrong angle."
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "label": "B",
    "display": "$\\dfrac{8}{15}$"
  },
  "solution": {
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "angles",
        "kind": "concept",
        "title": "Watch the angles",
        "caption": "**Watch the angles!** Given: $\\sin A$. Asked: $\\tan B$.",
        "lines": []
      },
      {
        "id": "known",
        "kind": "concept",
        "title": "Use the given ratio",
        "caption": "**SOH** CAH TOA: $\\sin = \\dfrac{\\mathrm{opposite}}{\\mathrm{hypotenuse}}$. From $A$, the opposite side is $BC$.",
        "note": "Any size has the same ratios, so use $BC = 15$, $AB = 17$.",
        "lines": [
          {
            "tex": "\\sin A = \\dfrac{BC}{AB} = \\dfrac{15}{17}",
            "kind": "chain_with_sides"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "triple",
        "kind": "concept",
        "title": "Shortcut: a Pythagorean triple",
        "caption": "**Shortcut:** $8$, $15$, $17$ is a Pythagorean triple.",
        "lines": [
          {
            "tex": "AC = 8",
            "kind": "chain_with_sides"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "missing",
        "kind": "simple",
        "title": "Check with the Pythagorean theorem",
        "caption": "No triple? Use the **Pythagorean theorem**.",
        "lines": [
          {
            "tex": "AC^2 = 17^2 - 15^2 = 64",
            "kind": "chain_with_sides"
          },
          {
            "tex": "AC = \\sqrt{64} = 8",
            "kind": "chain_with_sides"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "switch",
        "kind": "concept",
        "title": "Now look at angle B",
        "caption": "Now look at angle $B$: opposite and adjacent **switch**.",
        "lines": [
          {
            "tex": "\\text{opposite } B = AC = 8",
            "kind": "role_at_B",
            "role": "opposite"
          },
          {
            "tex": "\\text{adjacent } B = BC = 15",
            "kind": "role_at_B",
            "role": "adjacent"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "compute",
        "kind": "simple",
        "title": "Calculate tan B",
        "caption": "SOH CAH **TOA**: $\\tan = \\dfrac{\\mathrm{opposite}}{\\mathrm{adjacent}}$.",
        "lines": [
          {
            "tex": "\\tan B = \\dfrac{AC}{BC} = \\dfrac{8}{15}",
            "kind": "chain_with_sides"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "trap",
        "kind": "concept",
        "title": "The trap: tan A",
        "caption": "**The trap:** using angle $A$ gives $\\tan A$, choice D.",
        "lines": [
          {
            "tex": "\\tan A = \\dfrac{BC}{AC} = \\dfrac{15}{8}",
            "kind": "chain_with_sides"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "keyIdea": "Opposite and adjacent depend on **which angle** you use.",
    "trap": {
      "label": "D",
      "value": "15/8",
      "is": [
        "tan",
        "A"
      ]
    },
    "summary": "Watch the angles: the given ratio is sin A, but the question asks for tan B. sin A = 15/17 names two sides; any similar triangle has the same ratios, so use BC = 15 and AB = 17. 8, 15, 17 is a Pythagorean triple, so AC = 8; the Pythagorean theorem confirms it. From angle B the opposite side is AC = 8 and the adjacent side is BC = 15, so tan B = 8/15. Using angle A instead gives tan A = 15/8, the trap answer."
  },
  "meta": {
    "title_hook": "tan A or tan B? The Right-Triangle Trap",
    "description_lead": "In right triangle ABC, angle C = 90° and sin A = 15/17. What is tan B? Watch which angle you use."
  },
